# Build context is the repository root (see setup.conf), because the COPY paths
# below are repo-relative. BuildKit picks up this file because it sits next to
# the Dockerfile. Allowlist: everything is excluded except what the image needs,
# so secrets (settings.env), databases, tests and the other tool never reach the
# build context.
#
# The manifest entry must name this tool's own pyproject.toml. It used to be the
# repo-root one; after the split to per-tool manifests a stale `!pyproject.toml`
# left the file outside the context and the build failed on the bind-mount in
# the pip layer with "not found".
*
!crowdsec-metrics-exporter/pyproject.toml
!crowdsec-metrics-exporter/app/
!crowdsec-metrics-exporter/main.py
!crowdsec-metrics-exporter/docker/entrypoint.sh
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
